# Global Cursor Rules

## RTK - Rust Token Killer
Use rtk proxy for CLI dev operations to save tokens.
- Git and shell commands run through rtk proxy where supported.

## Git & PR Flow (Aarin / Consórcio)
- For MRs and branch creation, follow conventional commit format (e.g. feat:, fix:, chore:).
- Branches follow English naming with ticket/issue ID (e.g. feat/CLICKUP-123-description).
- PRs/MRs target DEV environment first.

## Graphify Knowledge Graph
- If graphify-out/graph.json exists:
  - Query codebase: graphify query "<question>"
  - Concept explanation: graphify explain "<concept>"
  - After modifying code, run graphify update . to keep graph current.

## Code Quality & Architecture
- Prefer explicit typing, modular decomposition, and single responsibility.
- Write tests alongside implementations.
